  - id: "project:project-bugreceipt:overview"
    category: project
    question: What is Montasim's BugReceipt project?
    text: "Montasim built BugReceipt, an extension project. Local-first Chrome extension for capturing privacy-filtered console, network, reproduction-step, and visual evidence in a reviewable bug report. His role covered product design and browser-extension engineering, with scope spanning capture lifecycle, privacy boundaries, review workflows, and release delivery. Reporters can preserve reproduction steps, bounded console and network evidence, environment details, and a recording or screenshot in one workflow. A hiring manager, developer, or client can use the linked case study to review the constraints, architecture, Montasim's contribution, and the result—not just the project summary."
    factIds[3]: "project:project-bugreceipt","case-study:bugreceipt:problem","case-study:bugreceipt:outcomes"
    supportingExcerpts[3]: "Local-first Chrome extension for capturing privacy-filtered console, network, reproduction-step, and visual evidence in a reviewable bug report.\n\nfalse\n2026-08-27T19:28:19Z\n396c58ff62a3ab2e23f2970cb54daed2bc3c9b1e\n2026-08-27T19:31:45Z\nhttps://github.com/montasim/BugReceipt\nproject-bugreceipt\nassets/projects/bugreceipt.png\nhttps://bugreceipt.netlify.app\n\nhttps://github.com/montasim/BugReceipt/releases/latest\nWXT\nReact 19\nTypeScript\nChrome Manifest V3\nChrome Extensions API\nTailwind CSS\nTanStack","Screenshots and vague descriptions rarely preserve the sequence, browser evidence, environment, and visual result developers need to reproduce a web application failure.\nBrowser diagnostics and screen recordings can expose sensitive information, while local filtering cannot guarantee that every secret will be recognized.\nChrome permission, selected-tab, service-worker, navigation, and storage boundaries must remain understandable during a capture.\nEmail delivery crosses a separate network boundary and must not","Reporters can preserve reproduction steps, bounded console and network evidence, environment details, and a recording or screenshot in one workflow.\nEvery captured item remains reviewable and removable before it leaves extension-owned storage.\nUsers can export a local Markdown-and-visual bundle or deliberately send a size-bounded report through the configured endpoint.\nMaintainers can exercise known failures and ship verifiable unpacked Chrome archives with published checksums."
  - id: "project:project-bugreceipt:technology"
    category: project
    question: Which technologies did Montasim use for BugReceipt?
    text: "Montasim built BugReceipt with WXT, React 19, TypeScript, Chrome Manifest V3, Chrome Extensions API, Tailwind CSS, TanStack Start, Zod, JSZip, Resend, Vitest, React Testing Library, Netlify, GitHub Actions, CI/CD, System Design. The product goal is clear: Local-first Chrome extension for capturing privacy-filtered console, network, reproduction-step, and visual evidence in a reviewable bug report. More importantly, the architecture is explicit: WXT Manifest V3 side panel, selected-tab recorder, review page, and background capture lifecycle; isolated page instrumentation feeding typed capture contracts; deterministic local privacy filtering and report rendering; extension storage and IndexedDB with local export or explicit Resend delivery through a TanStack Start endpoint. That gives technical reviewers a concrete system boundary to discuss instead of a list of framework keywords."
    factIds[2]: "project:project-bugreceipt","case-study:bugreceipt:architecture"
    supportingExcerpts[2]: "Local-first Chrome extension for capturing privacy-filtered console, network, reproduction-step, and visual evidence in a reviewable bug report.\n\nfalse\n2026-08-27T19:28:19Z\n396c58ff62a3ab2e23f2970cb54daed2bc3c9b1e\n2026-08-27T19:31:45Z\nhttps://github.com/montasim/BugReceipt\nproject-bugreceipt\nassets/projects/bugreceipt.png\nhttps://bugreceipt.netlify.app\n\nhttps://github.com/montasim/BugReceipt/releases/latest\nWXT\nReact 19\nTypeScript\nChrome Manifest V3\nChrome Extensions API\nTailwind CSS\nTanStack","Persistent React side panel, selected-tab recorder, manual steps, and editable review page.\nCapture interface\nBackground-owned capture lifecycle and Zod-validated extension message contracts.\nSession domain\nBounded local filtering with extension storage for session data and IndexedDB for visual evidence.\nPrivacy and storage\nMarkdown and visual report bundles stay local unless the user explicitly invokes the server-side Resend path.\nExport and delivery\nWXT Manifest V3 side panel, selected-tab recorder, review page,"
  - id: "project:project-shrnkly:overview"
    category: project
    question: What is Montasim's Shrnkly project?
    text: "Montasim built Shrnkly, a website project. Multilingual Next.js application for shortening URLs, sharing text, generating QR codes, and viewing basic usage analytics. His role covered product design and full-stack engineering, with scope spanning product workflows, data boundaries, and delivery. Users can shorten and track links. A hiring manager, developer, or client can use the linked case study to review the constraints, architecture, Montasim's contribution, and the result—not just the project summary."
    factIds[3]: "project:project-shrnkly","case-study:shrnkly:problem","case-study:shrnkly:outcomes"
    supportingExcerpts[3]: "Multilingual Next.js application for shortening URLs, sharing text, generating QR codes, and viewing basic usage analytics.\n\nfalse\n2025-06-16T05:25:05Z\n2653a830a22850be2144a63fe429f887acfc6f31\n2025-06-16T05:24:51Z\nhttps://github.com/montasim/shrnkly-url-shortener\nproject-shrnkly\nassets/projects/shrnkly.png\nhttps://shrnkly.netlify.app\n\nNext.js\nTypeScript\nMongoDB\nPrisma\nnext-intl\nQRCode\nReact Hook Form\nZod\nJest\nREST APIs\nReact\nTailwind CSS\nGitHub Actions\nGit\nSystem","Sharing links, expiring text/code, and QR payloads often requires separate tools and gives users little control over slugs, access, expiry, or basic view/click records.\nPassword protection is application access control, not safe secret storage.\nClick/view logging has privacy and retention implications.\nInstalled Redis and checked-in Docker artifacts are not documented as active/reliable runtime paths.","Users can shorten and track links.\nShare bounded text/code.\nCreate reusable QR payloads.\nApply supported access and lifecycle controls while understanding their privacy limits."
  - id: "project:project-shrnkly:technology"
