    text: "Montasim built Shrnkly with Next.js, TypeScript, MongoDB, Prisma, next-intl, QRCode, React Hook Form, Zod, Jest, REST APIs, React, Tailwind CSS, GitHub Actions, Git, System Design. The product goal is clear: Multilingual Next.js application for shortening URLs, sharing text, generating QR codes, and viewing basic usage analytics. More importantly, the architecture is explicit: Next.js localized URL/text/QR UI; server actions/routes for creation, redirect, and access checks; Prisma/MongoDB persistence; authentication, validation, and QR/browser-share adapters. That gives technical reviewers a concrete system boundary to discuss instead of a list of framework keywords."
