  - id: "project:project-ramadan-clock:overview"
    category: project
    question: What is Montasim's Ramadan Clock project?
    text: "Montasim built Ramadan Clock, a website project. 🌙 District-aware Sehri and Iftar schedules for Bangladesh, with PDF exports and protected timetable management. Next.js, PostgreSQL, Prisma. His role covered product design and full-stack engineering, with scope spanning product workflows, data boundaries, and delivery. Visitors can check daily and full Ramadan schedules. A hiring manager, developer, or client can use the linked case study to review the constraints, architecture, Montasim's contribution, and the result—not just the project summary."
    factIds[3]: "project:project-ramadan-clock","case-study:ramadan-clock:problem","case-study:ramadan-clock:outcomes"
    supportingExcerpts[3]: "🌙 District-aware Sehri and Iftar schedules for Bangladesh, with PDF exports and protected timetable management. Next.js, PostgreSQL, Prisma.\n\nfalse\n2026-02-19T04:40:57Z\nda1ee826b06fb925d92fef33f40a8f28da29b1e4\n2026-02-19T09:47:00Z\nhttps://github.com/montasim/ramadan-clock\nproject-ramadan-clock\nassets/projects/ramadan-clock.png\nhttps://fasttimes.netlify.app\n\nNext.js\nTypeScript\nPostgreSQL\nPrisma\nTailwind CSS\nNextAuth\nAladhan API\njsPDF\nREST APIs\nReact\nshadcn/ui\nRadix UI\nZod\nVitest\nGitHub Actions\nCI/CD\nSystem","Sehri/Iftar schedules need a clear local-time public view and an auditable maintenance workflow because external prayer-time sources, district selection, and timetable corrections can change the result.\nCalculated times depend on source, method, location, and local authority.\nExternal fetching requires retry/rate limiting and must not overwrite validated data indiscriminately.\nDuplicate date/location rows and malformed bulk imports must be rejected.","Visitors can check daily and full Ramadan schedules.\nAdministrators can import/fetch/manage location data.\nDuplicate/malformed records are rejected.\nUsers can export schedules while seeing source/accuracy guidance."
