    supportingExcerpts[3]: "Admin Dashboard UI built with Shadcn and Next.js.\n\nfalse\n2025-01-20T04:52:31Z\n1287edc200127f4a20ae7a343531d6aaaa6ad5e7\n2025-12-21T01:36:12Z\nhttps://github.com/montasim/book-heaven\nproject-book-heaven\nassets/projects/book-heaven.png\nhttps://bookheavenbeta.vercel.app\n\nNext.js\nReact\nTypeScript\nPostgreSQL\nPrisma\nRedis\nBullMQ\nSocket.io\nStripe\nREST APIs\nTailwind CSS\nshadcn/ui\nRadix UI\nTanStack Query\nReact Hook Form\nResend\nZod\nSystem Design\nBook","Readers, communities, marketplace activity, library operations, and AI-assisted discovery are commonly split across separate systems with disconnected identity and catalog data.\nThe broad feature set has many service dependencies and is beta, not a turnkey production claim.\nReal-time messaging is optional and falls back to HTTP polling.\nAI, embeddings/pgvector, payments, email, Redis queues, Firebase, and Socket.IO each require separate configuration and operational review.","Readers can discover and organize books.\nUsers can participate in community and marketplace flows.\nAdministrators can operate catalog/library workflows.\nDeployments can add AI, queues, real-time, payment, and email capabilities incrementally."
