  - id: "project:project-github-readme-counter:overview"
    category: project
    question: What is Montasim's GitHub README Counter project?
    text: "Montasim built GitHub README Counter, an API project. Express service that increments a file-backed counter and returns the current value as a customizable SVG image. His role covered API design and backend engineering, with scope spanning HTTP delivery, state management, and SVG generation. Users can self-host an embeddable counter. A hiring manager, developer, or client can use the linked case study to review the constraints, architecture, Montasim's contribution, and the result—not just the project summary."
    factIds[3]: "project:project-github-readme-counter","case-study:github-readme-counter:problem","case-study:github-readme-counter:outcomes"
    supportingExcerpts[3]: "Express service that increments a file-backed counter and returns the current value as a customizable SVG image.\n\nfalse\n2024-06-25T12:31:13Z\n9e56d4f2204c5ec6366c5306f20404219739290c\n2024-06-25T10:48:55Z\nhttps://github.com/montasim/github-readme-counter\nproject-github-readme-counter\nhttps://github-readme-counter.onrender.com/count.svg\n\nNode.js\nExpress.js\nJavaScript\nSVG\nSystem Design\nGitHub README","README authors need an image-embeddable counter endpoint because Markdown cannot run application JavaScript or call an API and render arbitrary data directly.\nRequests from bots, caches, renderers, and refreshes are counted, so values are not unique-human analytics.\nFile persistence is single-process and can reset on ephemeral filesystems.\nThe endpoint has no authentication or documented rate limiting.","Users can self-host an embeddable counter.\nCustomize the generated badge.\nKeep separate counters by identifier.\nMonitor basic process health."
  - id: "project:project-github-readme-counter:technology"
