    question: Which technologies did Montasim use for GitHub README Counter?
    text: "Montasim built GitHub README Counter with Node.js, Express.js, JavaScript, SVG, System Design. The product goal is clear: Express service that increments a file-backed counter and returns the current value as a customizable SVG image. More importantly, the architecture is explicit: Express routes and query validation; in-memory/file counter store; escaped dynamic SVG renderer plus JSON health endpoint. That gives technical reviewers a concrete system boundary to discuss instead of a list of framework keywords."
