  - id: "case-study:devtools:architecture"
    category: case-study
    question: How did Montasim structure the DevTools solution?
    text: "A navigation registry acts as the catalog source of truth. Tool features own their tabs and logic, shared app infrastructure handles auth and storage, and route handlers isolate network and persistence work. A representative decision was “Make the catalog declarative”: The navigation registry is the single source for tool discovery, reducing drift between routes, menus, and command search. The value of this architecture is the reasoning behind it—Montasim connects a real constraint to an explicit boundary that another developer can review, test, and evolve."
