  - id: "case-study:devtools:delivery"
    category: case-study
    question: What did Montasim deliver and achieve with DevTools?
    text: "Montasim designed and implemented the searchable toolbox and its shared tool interaction patterns. He built local formatters and generators alongside network diagnostics and reference utilities. He added account sync, expiring shares, short links, webhook inspection, and database-backed saved items. He established TypeScript, lint, production-build, and GitHub Actions checks for changes targeting main. The resulting capabilities and outcomes are “More than 50 workflows are available through one catalog and command-search model”; “Common transformations can run without an account and without sending their current input to the server”; “Server-backed features add reuse and sharing without obscuring when data leaves the browser”; “The architecture supports both small local utilities and stateful workflows without forcing them through one execution path”. This gives a reviewer a traceable line from Montasim's implementation work to the product capabilities and limits that followed."
    factIds[2]: "case-study:devtools:contribution","case-study:devtools:outcomes"
    supportingExcerpts[2]: "Designed and implemented the searchable toolbox and its shared tool interaction patterns.\nBuilt local formatters and generators alongside network diagnostics and reference utilities.\nAdded account sync, expiring shares, short links, webhook inspection, and database-backed saved items.\nEstablished TypeScript, lint, production-build, and GitHub Actions checks for changes targeting main.","More than 50 workflows are available through one catalog and command-search model.\nCommon transformations can run without an account and without sending their current input to the server.\nServer-backed features add reuse and sharing without obscuring when data leaves the browser.\nThe architecture supports both small local utilities and stateful workflows without forcing them through one execution path."
