  - id: "case-study:thoughtline:problem"
    category: case-study
    question: What problem did Montasim address in the Thoughtline - LinkedIn Writing Assistant case study?
    text: "Writing a useful LinkedIn reply or post requires understanding the visible conversation while preserving the author's own voice, intent, and control. Montasim owned product design and browser-extension engineering, covering browser integration, provider workflows, and privacy. The solution also had to respect “LinkedIn page content is untrusted and must be bounded before entering prompts”; “OpenRouter, Gemini, and Groq keys are all required so the fixed free-only route can fall back without asking during a writing task”. This case is useful to hiring teams and clients because it shows how he discovers the technical and product constraints behind an apparently simple request."
