    question: What problem did Montasim address in the Ramadan Clock case study?
    text: "Sehri/Iftar schedules need a clear local-time public view and an auditable maintenance workflow because external prayer-time sources, district selection, and timetable corrections can change the result. Montasim owned product design and full-stack engineering, covering product workflows, data boundaries, and delivery. The solution also had to respect “Calculated times depend on source, method, location, and local authority”; “External fetching requires retry/rate limiting and must not overwrite validated data indiscriminately”. This case is useful to hiring teams and clients because it shows how he discovers the technical and product constraints behind an apparently simple request."
