    supportingExcerpts[3]: "May 18, 2026\nMd. Tamim Tanvir, MBA\nworked with Mohammad Montasim Al Mamun but on different teams\nSenior Product Designer | Healthcare SaaS & Telemedicine | HIPAA-aware, WCAG accessible | 8+ yrs\nI had the opportunity to work closely with Montasim at MyMedicalHub International Ltd., where I led UX/UI design for our telemedicine and SaaS healthcare platforms while he led frontend engineering.\n\nFrom a designer’s perspective, what makes Montasim different is that he understands frontend development as a systems","June 5, 2025\nMd. Sazzad Hossain\nworked with Mohammad Montasim Al Mamun on the same team\nSoftware Engineer | Next.js 16 & React 19 Architecture | Full-Stack & Real-Time Systems (WebRTC, Socket.io) | AI & Cloud\nI highly recommend Montasim as an exceptional Frontend Software Engineer. I had the pleasure of collaborating closely with Montasim on the Telemedicine project at MyMedicalHub International Ltd., where we both made significant contributions to the front-end development.\n\nMontasim's expertise in frontend","May 26, 2025\nMd. Rifaet Ullah\nworked with Mohammad Montasim Al Mamun but on different teams\nSoftware Engineer | Django | AI | Machine Learning | Microservice\nMontasim is the rare engineer who effortlessly bridges the gap between research and production. At MyMedicalHUB International Ltd., he integrated our AI-driven analysis pipeline into a seamless user experience, building components that showcased annotated pictures and metric visualizations in real time. His passion for clean code and deep understanding of"
  - id: "hiring-fit-due-diligence:client-project-fit"
    category: hiring-fit-due-diligence
    question: Why might a client choose Montasim for a complex web product?
    text: "A client would get an engineer who can move from requirements and hidden constraints into architecture, implementation, testing, and reviewable outcomes. Montasim can demonstrate that process across SaaS, AI, browser extensions, data products, packages, and developer tools; his Codez role also directly records analyzing client needs, implementing the required functionality, and executing test scenarios. The best fit is a project that values clear technical boundaries and dependable delivery, not just rapid screen production."
    factIds[3]: "experience:experience-codez-web-developer","project:project-postcraft","case-study:postcraft:outcomes"
    supportingExcerpts[3]: "Codez Info Tech.\n\nDeveloped and maintained **web applications with PHP and JavaScript**. Analyzed **client needs** and developed appropriate functionality. Created and executed **test scenarios** to ensure quality deliverables.\nexperience-codez-web-developer\nNorth Badda, Dhaka, Bangladesh\nC\n/images/organizations/codez.png\nMay 2021 - Nov 2021\nWeb Developer\nPHP\nJavaScript\nHTML\nCSS","AI-powered social media manager to generate, preview, score, and auto-publish engaging posts for LinkedIn, X, and Facebook using Gemini AI and custom brand guardrails.\n\ntrue\n2026-05-21T22:57:30Z\n664e1557c35eebde3bdb3a106447b4716e103b2c\n2026-05-26T16:29:25Z\nhttps://github.com/montasim/PostCraft\nproject-postcraft\nassets/projects/postcraft.png\nhttps://aipostcraft.vercel.app\n\nNext.js\nReact\nTypeScript\nMongoDB\nMongoose\nRedux Toolkit\nBetter Auth\nOpenRouter\nGemini API\nGroq API\nZhipuAI\nInngest\nREST APIs\nTailwind","One workspace now covers generation, comparison, refinement, preview, and delivery.\nProvider and key fallback reduce the workflow's dependency on a single AI endpoint.\nPublishing state is persisted for library and insights views instead of ending at generation.\nOperational limits remain explicit: publishing still depends on platform approval, scopes, account type, and API access."
  - id: "hiring-fit-due-diligence:startup-fit"
    category: hiring-fit-due-diligence
    question: What makes Montasim relevant to a fast-moving startup?
    text: "His portfolio shows breadth without losing delivery discipline: frontend and backend work, AI-provider integration, product experiments, CI/CD, cloud-cost ownership, and a broad independent-project record. The strongest evidence is his ability to turn ambiguous product constraints into explicit boundaries and testable outcomes."
    factIds[4]: profile,"experience:experience-mymedicalhub-software-engineer","case-study:thoughtline:architecture","case-study:postcraft:outcomes"
    supportingExcerpts[4]: "Most software looks great in the demo. I build the kind that survives production.\n\nI'm a **Senior Software Engineer** with **3+ years** building real-time, AI-driven, multi-tenant SaaS platforms across the full stack: React, Next.js, Node.js, and TypeScript. Promoted twice at the same company, I now own frontend architecture across a multi-service platform, lead PR reviews, and mentor the engineers behind me.\n\nKey highlights: cut cloud infrastructure costs **70%** by migrating Azure VMs to App Service with","MyMedicalHub International Ltd.\nhttps://mymedicalhub.com\nBoosted application performance by **40%** by stripping legacy UI libraries and optimizing React rendering cycles. Achieved **70% infrastructure cost reduction** by migrating Azure VMs to App Service and automating CI/CD pipelines. Deployed a **HIPAA-compliant SSO system** with multi-role access, OAuth integration, and strict CSP headers.\nexperience-mymedicalhub-software-engineer\nMohakhali, Dhaka, Bangladesh\nM\n/images/organizations/mymedicalhub.png\nOct 2023","LinkedIn content scripts/extraction plus bounded manual pasted-post input.\nPage integration\nReact side-panel workflows.\nExtension interface\nTyped drafting/source-research ports with curated free OpenRouter models, bounded provider timeouts, and Gemini/Groq fallback.\nProvider boundary\nEncrypted browser storage, migrations, backup/export, and Manifest V3 permissions.\nStorage and delivery\nLinkedIn content scripts plus manual pasted-post input; React side-panel workflows; typed drafting/source-research ports with free","One workspace now covers generation, comparison, refinement, preview, and delivery.\nProvider and key fallback reduce the workflow's dependency on a single AI endpoint.\nPublishing state is persisted for library and insights views instead of ending at generation.\nOperational limits remain explicit: publishing still depends on platform approval, scopes, account type, and API access."
