  - id: "hiring-fit-due-diligence:ambiguity-handling"
    category: hiring-fit-due-diligence
    question: How does Montasim approach ambiguous engineering problems?
    text: "His case studies start by separating the visible feature from underlying constraints, then document boundaries, decisions, contribution, and outcomes. Thoughtline distinguishes page input, providers, credentials, and publish control; PostCraft separates request-time editing from durable scheduling. That is strong evidence of structured ambiguity reduction."
    factIds[3]: "case-study:thoughtline:problem","case-study:thoughtline:architecture","case-study:postcraft:architecture"
    supportingExcerpts[3]: "Writing a useful LinkedIn reply or post requires understanding the visible conversation while preserving the author's own voice, intent, and control.\nLinkedIn page content is untrusted and must be bounded before entering prompts.\nOpenRouter, Gemini, and Groq keys are all required so the fixed free-only route can fall back without asking during a writing task.\nExtension permissions, encrypted local storage, and retention/export behavior must remain understandable to the user.","LinkedIn content scripts/extraction plus bounded manual pasted-post input.\nPage integration\nReact side-panel workflows.\nExtension interface\nTyped drafting/source-research ports with curated free OpenRouter models, bounded provider timeouts, and Gemini/Groq fallback.\nProvider boundary\nEncrypted browser storage, migrations, backup/export, and Manifest V3 permissions.\nStorage and delivery\nLinkedIn content scripts plus manual pasted-post input; React side-panel workflows; typed drafting/source-research ports with free","Generation, scoring, editing, brand rules, and platform previews\nWorkspace\nValidated workflows for content, library, accounts, and publishing\nDomain services\nOpenRouter, Groq, Gemini, and ZhipuAI with model and key fallback\nProvider layer\nMongoDB persistence, Inngest jobs, and social platform APIs\nDelivery\nThe Next.js application keeps HTTP boundaries in route handlers, product logic in domain modules, infrastructure in core services, and durable delivery in Inngest.\nA provider switcher walks configured models and"
  - id: "hiring-fit-due-diligence:quality-discipline"
    category: hiring-fit-due-diligence
    question: What evidence shows Montasim values engineering quality?
    text: "The record includes automated testing, PR reviews, deterministic state, strict validation boundaries, performance measurement, and case studies that state limitations instead of hiding them. A QA colleague also describes clean, maintainable code, attention to detail, structured problem-solving, and consistent high-quality delivery."
