    supportingExcerpts[3]: "MyMedicalHub International Ltd.\nhttps://mymedicalhub.com\nArchitected an **FSM-based biometric engine** replacing unstable React hooks with deterministic state transitions for **99.9% reliability** during AI analysis. Optimized **AI pipelines** to support **60 FPS** pose estimation and real-time rep counting via adaptive frame rate logic. Led a full rewrite of the **medical assessment chatbot** with Redux Toolkit and refactored **54+ modules** into Presentational/Container","Real-Time & Computer Vision\nskills-realtime-vision\nWebRTC\nOpentok\nMediaPipe","October 7, 2022\nAbu Saleh Musa Miah\nwas Mohammad Montasim Al Mamun’s teacher\nWorld’s Top 2% Scientist, IEEE Senior Member, Post-Doctoral Researcher in the Graduate Dept. of Computer Science and Engineering at the University of Aizu\nDear all,\nMOHAMMAD MONTASIM-AL-MAMUN SHUVO was my student, and I was his undergraduate thesis supervisor unofficially. We worked together on a range of tough projects, such as Driver drowsiness detection, Hand pose detection and many others projects. All of the projects he completed"
  - id: "technical-depth:adaptive-webgl"
    category: technical-depth
    question: How did Montasim prevent Foliofarer's 3D interface from excluding users?
    text: "Foliofarer keeps core career content and navigation independent from WebGL, adds an accessible Atlas path, stores Passport progress locally, and adapts rendering to device capability and user preferences. The architecture treats 3D as an enhancement rather than the only route to the information."
    factIds[2]: "project:project-foliofarer","case-study:foliofarer:architecture"
    supportingExcerpts[2]: "Foliofarer is an interactive 3D developer portfolio built with Next.js, React Three Fiber, Three.js and TypeScript, featuring an accessible career Atlas, local Passport progress and adaptive WebGL rendering.\n\nfalse\n2026-08-11T04:55:39Z\n358c8036ebd35b75398baa5463b6acd445356533\n2026-08-11T04:54:55Z\nhttps://github.com/montasim/foliofarer\nproject-foliofarer\nassets/projects/foliofarer.png\nhttps://foliofarer.netlify.app\n\nNext.js\nReact\nTypeScript\nReact Three Fiber\nThree.js\nDrei\nReact Three Rapier\nTailwind","Next.js route shell and accessible Atlas.\nInterface\nReact Three Fiber/Three.js scene runtime and Rapier interaction.\nDomain\nDeterministic journey compiler/generators and validated portfolio data.\nData and integrations\nPlaywright/unit/visual contracts plus static assets.\nQuality and delivery\nNext.js route shell and accessible Atlas; React Three Fiber/Three.js scene runtime and Rapier interaction; deterministic journey compiler/generators and validated portfolio data; Playwright/unit/visual contracts plus static"
  - id: "technical-depth:developer-tool-scale"
    category: technical-depth
    question: How did Montasim avoid building a separate architecture for every DevTools utility?
    text: "The DevTools case study defines shared contracts for tool metadata, validation, execution, state, and presentation, while keeping local transformations distinct from server-backed features. That lets more than 50 workflows share platform behavior without forcing unrelated tools into one implementation."
    factIds[3]: "project:project-devtools","case-study:devtools:architecture","case-study:devtools:outcomes"
    supportingExcerpts[3]: "A comprehensive suite of 30+ free developer tools for formatting, validating, generating, and transforming data. All tools run entirely in your browser.\n\ntrue\n2026-04-08T05:59:03Z\n88e28b53c9c618f016edbaada4918442f070d25e\n2026-04-12T09:19:56Z\nhttps://github.com/montasim/devtools\nproject-devtools\nassets/projects/devtools.png\nhttps://devtoolsn.vercel.app\n\nNext.js\nReact\nTypeScript\nCodeMirror 6\nTanStack Query\nPostgreSQL\nPrisma\nBetter Auth\nTailwind CSS\nshadcn/ui\nRadix UI\nZod\nVitest\nGitHub Actions\nCI/CD\nSystem","Searchable navigation, routes, labels, and keyboard discovery\nTool registry\nFocused formatters, generators, testers, inspectors, and references\nFeature modules\nLocal transforms, preferences, input history, and reusable state\nBrowser boundary\nNext.js APIs, Better Auth, PostgreSQL, Prisma, and target services\nServer boundary\nA navigation registry acts as the catalog source of truth. Tool features own their tabs and logic, shared app infrastructure handles auth and storage, and route handlers isolate network and","More than 50 workflows are available through one catalog and command-search model.\nCommon transformations can run without an account and without sending their current input to the server.\nServer-backed features add reuse and sharing without obscuring when data leaves the browser.\nThe architecture supports both small local utilities and stateful workflows without forcing them through one execution path."
